{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe","id":774478,"title":"Apocalypse: The Fall of a Tribe..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-25T19:28:03-08:00","id":774478,"title":"Apocalypse: The Fall of a Tribe..","content":"..To the Wyrm option.<br /> Imagine you're running (or perhaps you already have) the Apocalypse end of things scenarios and you go with the idea of a Tribe of Garou falling to the Wyrm begore the final battle (and kicking off a lot of bad things in the process). What tribe would you choose to fall? And why?<br /> <br /> In the first game I ran for Apocalypse I chose the Children of Gaia. I called in 'The Death of Hope'. Thinking the group would freak out about the corruption and fall of these cleansers and supporters of peace, unity, love, hope etc. But I think everyone was more worried about losing so many npcs that could likely of had mothers touch <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the Second game I ran I used the Red Talons, who after saying good byes to a few caerns and singing howls of extinctions to more creatures hunted beyond saving just lost it. That scared everyone. So much the wanted more city stories rather thsn in the wild just in case wyrm fallen talon or three turned up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm looking to run another soon...and I'm considering using the StarGazers. Harano creeps in under the weight of their own meditations. They left there cousins for the beast courts in the hopes that they could make a difference. They did, now they see in the guilt and depression how they have damned their brethren to die and the beast courts are no better. They looked so deep within and saw the wyrm within themselves and stopped looking at the wyrm around them or something like that perhaps. Like the children of gaia for hope, I see something truly terrible in the most insightful of all of gaias tribes falling first. <br /> <br /> Which tribe would you choose? And why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T20:40:37-08:00","id":774512,"title":"","content":"Silent Striders; cast out from their ancestral home, plagued by the dead, constantly a visitor in other peoples territory. They have the longest run of crap luck and the fact that they are still considered a tribe is astounding. Falling to the wyrm could give them something Gaia hasn't in a long time, Hope. They could break their their curse and take back their home, ride out their last days finally with some peace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:17:17-08:00","id":774524,"title":"","content":"Bonegnawers, tired of being shit on by they decide to get on the winning team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T00:24:14-08:00","id":774579,"title":"","content":"Red Talons, they were always the closest to the edge and the most separated from the other tribes. History has shown that the tribes who are the most distant and isolationist tend to be the ones that have bad things happen to them. The Garou were meant to act as one, with many perspectives and opinions to temper their instincts, but the Talons have cut themselves off from all those filthy goddamn homid-lovers for too long. Couple that with the fact that they're probably right more often than anyone would be willing to admit, because admitting it would be admitting to the logic of genocide, and you have a witches brew of potential for a fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:02:17-08:00","id":774596,"title":"","content":"I love Apocalypse. It's a brilliant book. But I really cannot bring myself to run an Ending chronicle, It's supposed to be legendary and epic, and I'm not sure how do you go back to it once you've done it. I'm surprised to hear people have actually done it multiple times, and with that specific scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:02:20-08:00","id":774597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774512#post774512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silent Striders; cast out from their ancestral home, plagued by the dead, constantly a visitor in other peoples territory. They have the longest run of crap luck and the fact that they are still considered a tribe is astounding. Falling to the wyrm could give them something Gaia hasn't in a long time, Hope. They could break their their curse and take back their home, ride out their last days finally with some peace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh yeah. Of course the Wyrm is lying about peace, and once they get a chance to reclaim their land the world is full of death and the dead. The maelstrom brings in hundreds of thousands of wraiths and angry spectres that the striders use with the wyrms powers of command and coersion to curse hex and tear into the living and wreak despairing vengeance. Meanwhile Set just smiles to himself.<br /> <br /> ok, I may be sold on this to use too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:05:21-08:00","id":774601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774524#post774524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonegnawers, tired of being shit on by they decide to get on the winning team.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bonegnawers seem to be bigger favourite all around than I first realised. Seeing them fall and eat the flesj of the dead and the weak as cities fall and the wyld burns is so good as the Scavengers of Rust and decay make their walk to the top of the apocalyptic trash pile. Perhaps ironic that once they do so, theu find themselves beneath the Spirals. Ohh like this. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:15:04-08:00","id":774608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774579#post774579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red Talons, they were always the closest to the edge and the most separated from the other tribes. History has shown that the tribes who are the most distant and isolationist tend to be the ones that have bad things happen to them. The Garou were meant to act as one, with many perspectives and opinions to temper their instincts, but the Talons have cut themselves off from all those filthy goddamn homid-lovers for too long. Couple that with the fact that they're probably right more often than anyone would be willing to admit, because admitting it would be admitting to the logic of genocide, and you have a witches brew of potential for a fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much what I did in my second apocalypse campaign. I love the talons but yes their isolations and constant losses to the ever growing encroachment of humanity and the extintion of whole species of beasts proved too much. I had it start with the fall of three RT caerns, new laws on wolf hunting being acceoted, and the loss of a whole state of wolf breeding stock due to very effective poison and trapping campaign (cough pentex helped). Which lead to the RTs demanding a new impergium and aid to reclaim their lands and push back the evil homids. When every tribe said no, it was the last straw and the wyrm whispered to them how many humans must die and which areas would be the best to attack to affect the human population enough to make wolves the dominant creature in the food chain once again. Which they did by realeasing some of the most dangerous bound wyld spirits into maws of wyrm elements of cataclysm and destruction and suffering. Basically creating brand new versions of the storm eater to wipe out everything. Was really sad and brutal. Great players in that one made it truly epic, I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:24:10-08:00","id":774611,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8760_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8760\" data-vbnamecard=\"8760\">Cogliostro</a> (because for some reason I cant quote your post???) I agree it is a great book. I've run a few stories of it (only two to the finish as the players asked nicely not to finish it and risk dying and just leave it vague and unaswered. Cowards. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No thats totally a fair request considering the love that grow for a pc I feel), my reason being is because its not only a world event, its a universe event. Each one starts in different area, different country, different types of septs and caerns and of course different characters that go through it. Each time its different, even though the backdrop is the same. My hope is to eventually have a moment from each game I've run colliding together. Invite all the players who ever played in one to bring their favourite characters and all play together in one giant showdown. If one character goes down, then you pick up another aheet for a different chatacter and push on! Till the end! For the Nation! For Gaia!<br /> <br /> And then show them what I have in mind for After Apocalypse. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T10:53:43-08:00","id":774911,"title":"","content":"I'd REALLY like to do a Children of Gaia trying to do an overthrow over the garou Nation plot, myself. A subtle try at converting ancestor spirits/reincarnation and when that doesn't work, try an utter overthrow.<br /> <br /> After which they join the Dancers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T12:55:49-08:00","id":774978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774601#post774601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonegnawers seem to be bigger favourite all around than I first realised.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bone Gnawers would be the obvious choice for me. So much in canon shows them to be susceptible to falling to the Wyrm. There is a large percentage of them that aren't participating the tribe or septs. Many are angry and resentful against the greater Garou Nation. Even upstanding members supposedly have dealings with Leeches and who knows what else. Furthermore, I've thought that the Maneaters camp is essentially what a &quot;fallen&quot; BG tribe would become. Not only do I think the tribe could fall to the Wyrm in numbers (and wipe out the Gaian Bone Gnawers like what was done with the White Howlers), but I think it is conceivable the Rat totem could fall.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T12:57:22-08:00","id":774979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774596#post774596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Apocalypse. It's a brilliant book. But I really cannot bring myself to run an Ending chronicle, It's supposed to be legendary and epic, and I'm not sure how do you go back to it once you've done it. I'm surprised to hear people have actually done it multiple times, and with that specific scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't something I have much interest in either, although I could see why a group of hardcore Werewolf players might want to run it.<br /> <br /> I like the eschatological feel in the setting that this may be the last days more than having Doomsday actually arrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T13:10:20-08:00","id":774989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774911#post774911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd REALLY like to do a Children of Gaia trying to do an overthrow over the garou Nation plot, myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is some good potential that the Children of Gaia are more susceptible to the Wyrm then what may be apparent. They are not good candidates for the moustache twirling, no hands washing style of evil too often depicted for the Wyrm. However, the combination of sanctimoniousness, naivety, and constant criticism of their own people put them in the same kind of category of real world people who supported Marxism and then wonder what is going on with all these gulags, genocide, and mass repression. <br /> <br /> The only thing missing (besides a &quot;Bolshevik&quot; inner core within the tribe) is how Wyrm worship would become open - I think it would have to be done in stages without the members realizing they serve the Wyrm. Perhaps all the burned out hippies in the Tribe going on a bad drug induced trip that ends up being the equivalent of walking the spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T14:33:59-08:00","id":775031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774911#post774911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd REALLY like to do a Children of Gaia trying to do an overthrow over the garou Nation plot, myself. A subtle try at converting ancestor spirits/reincarnation and when that doesn't work, try an utter overthrow.<br /> <br /> After which they join the Dancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow Lords and Children of Gaia are my two favourite tribes. I love the idea of the Coggies going 'no enough is enough. We will bring the purity of peace upon you. Through destruction, so gaias spirit will have a chance to go on after .' And the shadow lords being very syrprised that they never saw it coming. Or that the coggies could do it so well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T14:37:00-08:00","id":775032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774978#post774978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Bone Gnawers would be the obvious choice for me. So much in canon shows them to be susceptible to falling to the Wyrm. There is a large percentage of them that aren't participating the tribe or septs. Many are angry and resentful against the greater Garou Nation. Even upstanding members supposedly have dealings with Leeches and who knows what else. Furthermore, I've thought that the Maneaters camp is essentially what a &amp;quot;fallen&amp;quot; BG tribe would become. Not only do I think the tribe could fall to the Wyrm in numbers (and wipe out the Gaian Bone Gnawers like what was done with the White Howlers), but I think it is conceivable the Rat totem could fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this too. Yeah, after all the losses Rat has suffered I dont imagine it would take much to push king rat over the edge to wyrm. Or make it be enough so it could never be rescued, by killing off Mother Rat for example. Harsh but epic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T14:40:46-08:00","id":775038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=774989#post774989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there is some good potential that the Children of Gaia are more susceptible to the Wyrm then what may be apparent. They are not good candidates for the moustache twirling, no hands washing style of evil too often depicted for the Wyrm. However, the combination of sanctimoniousness, naivety, and constant criticism of their own people put them in the same kind of category of real world people who supported Marxism and then wonder what is going on with all these gulags, genocide, and mass repression. <br /> <br /> The only thing missing (besides a &amp;quot;Bolshevik&amp;quot; inner core within the tribe) is how Wyrm worship would become open - I think it would have to be done in stages without the members realizing they serve the Wyrm. Perhaps all the burned out hippies in the Tribe going on a bad drug induced trip that ends up being the equivalent of walking the spiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they go there willingly. Believing with sacrifice they can return the wyrm back to its natural pure state. Defeating the three heads at once. Turns out they are right. They just have to sacrifice all the other tribes to the wyrm first. So they will all be children of gaia in the next life. Or some other crazy scheme. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T16:43:05-08:00","id":775093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=775031#post775031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Shadow Lords and Children of Gaia are my two favourite tribes. I love the idea of the Coggies going 'no enough is enough. We will bring the purity of peace upon you. Through destruction, so gaias spirit will have a chance to go on after .' And the shadow lords being very syrprised that they never saw it coming. Or that the coggies could do it so well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, exactly. Silent Strider revised really made me rethink the tribe, when it's narrator offered a more cynical take on them. And it is very right, the Coggies play politics very well. After all, they are trusted to tend the land, trusted to heal,etc. Also, seen as harmless most of the time.<br /> <br /> Yet, how easy would it be for them to start actively converting garou? How likely is it that they all ready -are-? Maybe for good, but good intentions can lead to bad results easily. And all the cast off from other tribes, all the metis taken in, how loyal they all are. Clearly, Unicorn's Children have the right idea. So if the foolish other tribes can't see it, they will be -made- to see it. Not by violence, but by conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T21:45:32-08:00","id":775241,"title":"","content":"I have often toyed with having a different tribe fall to the Wyrm in place of the White Howlers. <br /> The list in order with a thought or two:<br /> Children of Gaia: The master spies of the Garou Nation peddling peace and unity while being utterly ineffective except in stirring up discord. The Garou Nation rocked by this betrayal actually become more unified the War of Tears and War of Rage 2 still happen but both are driven by the fear the Bunyip who are isolated are in danger of falling to the Howls of Darkness. And the other breeds will find out the shame of the nation.<br /> The Silver Fangs furious at the lesser tribes the Fangs attempt to become absolute rulers the Tribe fractured and took a portion of the Nation with them as they fell. The newly formed Blood Omegas wage a constant war with the Nation War of Tears still happens as the conflict sweeps through Australia. <br /> The Nation being on the defensive has resulted in stronger ties to the other Changing Breeds as the Nation has sought allies in the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T02:24:38-08:00","id":775330,"title":"","content":"@Ana: I like this. I'll be honest and say I didnt think too much, or pay much attention to the Coggies when the first ed core book and players guide came out. It wasnt until I read the First Ed CoG Tribe book came out that I actually gave them a second thought. It's how aware and dedicated they were to the defeat and destruction of the Defiler Wyrm that made me aee just how on the ball insightfully and how dedicated they were to being the very opposite of it opposition and defiance. <br /> Then I realised 'Holy Gaia! The are the opposites of the wyrm Triat itself. Promoting and striving for Peace in opposition of War. Encouraging Unity and Healing, Purity and protection of the weak in opposition to the Defiler. And Fertility, Hope, against the Eater of Souls.<br /> which all takes a lot of internal strength and devotion to do, especially in a race as brutal and fierce as the Garou. My hat goes off to any Coggie looking to uphold those ideals. Which I've had fun playing and watching others reactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T02:54:49-08:00","id":775346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774478-apocalypse-the-fall-of-a-tribe?p=775241#post775241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have often toyed with having a different tribe fall to the Wyrm in place of the White Howlers. <br /> The list in order with a thought or two:<br /> Children of Gaia: The master spies of the Garou Nation peddling peace and unity while being utterly ineffective except in stirring up discord. The Garou Nation rocked by this betrayal actually become more unified the War of Tears and War of Rage 2 still happen but both are driven by the fear the Bunyip who are isolated are in danger of falling to the Howls of Darkness. And the other breeds will find out the shame of the nation.<br /> The Silver Fangs furious at the lesser tribes the Fangs attempt to become absolute rulers the Tribe fractured and took a portion of the Nation with them as they fell. The newly formed Blood Omegas wage a constant war with the Nation War of Tears still happens as the conflict sweeps through Australia. <br /> The Nation being on the defensive has resulted in stronger ties to the other Changing Breeds as the Nation has sought allies in the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh a Different tribe other than the White b Howlers. Interesting, I like it!<br /> Making it the Children of Gaia is really horrorfied too. I think it would make things all around worse b for everything and everyone on epic levels depending on how it would be run with.<br /> <br /> I'd run it truly a darker reflection than the game currently knows. That in their fall in the Dark Ages the Children of Gaia then captured and corrupted their old patron Unicorn and under the banner of the Wyrm arose the Orphans of Creation.<br /> <br /> Hope, Purity, Fertility, Peace, Unity, Healing. ..the Epithilings and old brood of Unicorn took it hardest in the spirit realms. With new dischord, disease and death spreading far and wide. <br /> The garou lost their greatest healers and with it, hope for the future became a childish dream.<br /> <br /> Englings have become the rarest spirits to find now, and the Orphans twisted rites of fertility have born an increase in new banes and fomor never before imagined.<br /> <br /> The Orphans will become a major factor in the world by the modern day as their totem the twisted Unicorn breathes Balefire in the name of War, blights the land and hearts of others in its wake for the Defiler and rains down despair and hopelessness for the Eater of Souls to gain nourishment from as breeder banes and their fomori kinfolk churn out new horrors in the name of The Father in mockery of Gaia.<br /> <br /> ohh okay now I have more ideas...unicorn horsemen of the Apocalypse anyone? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T06:53:35-08:00","id":775954,"title":"","content":"Why let fall only one tribe? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> My evil plan (that will never see fruition, as I got no players) would see the fall of 4 tribes (obviously, not all the pups of fallen tribes fall themselves).<br /> 1st stage: Get of Fenris<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whitewolf Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">After discovering a series of underground cave networks that lead to the Black Spiral Hive, the Get mount a massive assault on their enemy. But as the Get travel further into the tunnels, they go deeper and deeper into the earth as the Spirals pick off the Get less likely to fall. The Get in the tunnels begin to experience a variety of visions that slowly drive them mad, and they fall to the Wyrm. On the first full moon of the month, they lead an all out assault on the Garou of Europe, destroying or desecrating Caerns and eventually slaughter the Shadow Lords. The Get are renamed The Pure, and their totem, Great Fenris, is chained up in Malfeas, never falling.</div> </div> </div> </div>mostly as canon, but the Get were in the beginning fewer than the Shadow Lords, let alone all the Garou in Europe, and they probably suffered losses from their underground assaulte. In the end, while killing roughly a several hundreds European Garou (mostly, Lords) they are exterminated.<br /> <br /> 2nd stage, part 1:Fianna<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whitewolf Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Former Ard Righ Brendan O'Rourke returns from an Umbral quest into Malfeas where he had been turned to the Wyrm. He brings back massive reinforcements for an assault on the British Isles. He strikes at several Fianna holdings and even convinces many of the other Garou tribes that the non-fallen Fianna are the ones who are of the Wyrm. They do not realize the deception until it is too late, by this point Garou have been fighting Garou until only a few thousand still survive. The Fianna become the Black Stags, but Stag their totem does not fall, nor does he cut off his fallen children. Some Black Stags follow Whipporwill and some follow other Wyrmish Incarnae spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>While spared from the Get onslaught, the Fianna are reduced to only a fraction of themselves. Turning to the Wyrm they actually got possess of all the Britain caerns. But...<br /> <br /> 2nd stage, part 2:Red Talons<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whitewolf Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A disease similar to Mad Cow infects the Red Talons due to the consumption of Human flesh. While the disease has little harm on the Garou, it is devastating to their wolf Kin. Within a short span of time the infection spreads killing more than 90% of wolves in the world, making wolves all but extinct with no chance of ever recovering. The Talons blame the humans for this and decide to kill them all, by communicating with ancient spirits deep in the earth to release methane gasses trapped deep in the earth into the atmosphere, dooming billions of humans. The Talons new name is the Predators. Griffin, mad with Rage, remains their totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Talons fall, and fall bad :P<br /> But, one of their firsts methane traps is released near a major hive of the fallen Fianna. As the Wyrm is not famous for its internal order or communication between its parts, the Fianna quickly wage war on the Red Talons. Only some hundreds Garou of these two Tribes survive this &quot;internal&quot; strife.<br /> <br /> 3nd stage:Glass Walkers<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whitewolf Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Walkers tribal totem, Cockroach, strikes a deal with the Corporate Spirit Incarna of Pentex, essentially offering the tribe and totem positions of safety during and after the Apocalypse. The Glass Walkers, now calling themselves the Raiders, maintain their connection with the Gaian tribes, hiding their taint with wolf-skins until they are discovered to have kidnapped the Perfect Metis, which eventually leads to the Final Battle. The Pentex Incarna is consumed by an avatar of the Wyrm, and becomes a Celestine and controls all the employees of Pentex as a massive powerful hive mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar to this description, but the Walkers fall to the Weaver, slowly becoming Drones, until in the last battleground they make their stand among the Weaver ranks. As some form of free thought seems to remain in them, in the Last Battle they mostly target the Wyrm and the Spiral Dancers dragging most of the Weaver forces behind them and making their last fight truly epic, actually giving a real chance to the Garou Nation.<br /> Will remain unclear if this was their plan from the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:33:29-08:00","id":776139,"title":"","content":"I would also choose a multi-tribal fall. Actually I fully intend on doing it next time I run Werewolf.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't damn just four tribes. I would see all of them in the Wyrms side.<br /> <br /> First of all, the Silver Fangs. They where used by the Wyrm before, more than any other tribe. Their pride and prejudice are greater than any other, if less direct than Get's. They leaded the Nation until now, but under their ideas the Werewolf destroied their chances instead of increase them. So finaly Falcon lift the curse of madness and tries to give them clarity. But instead of the scenario where they readilly fall and slaughter the Dancers, they become far more insidious in a slow fall, and foster the fall of the other tribes.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the Garou Nation as a whole is on the verge of falling anyway. Too much problems. Not nearly enough hope. And each tribe to fall can deliver precisely the strike to fell another one. The Furies love the Wyld, but they also hate too much things, and most of them follow hate more than love, war more than wisdom. The Bone Gnawers did their job for centuries without any reward except be left alone in the best of times. The Children of Gaia just lost their time with a bunch that never, EVER listened to them, and watched in horror as the Nation did the job of the Wyrm in more than one occasion. The Fianna are remnants of a time that won't come back, and the more they want to be seen as fearsome warriors, an increasing number of them are just lazy bullies. The Get of Fenris is already much of the Wyrm as far as I would say, it would be more a formalization and a (little) change of targets. The Glass Walkers are too out of tune with the greater picture, and too confident. The Red Talons, sorry for the eople who likes then, but they are even more of the Wyrm than the Get. The Shadow Lords allways played too much close to corruption (and undeniably corrupted in some cases). The Silent Striders already suffered too much, and just a chance to take vengeance on Set is enough to their fall. Uktena and Wendigo where once the Pure Tribes, but now they are far from this.<br /> <br /> What I won't make is a cohesive fall. They won't be friends on the Wyrm's side, but instead be more open on their own hate of each other. Some won't fall to the Wyrm, but to the Weaver, on an individual basis (with some cases, as Furies and Talons, being fatalists who threw up their love for the Wyld and hate against the Weaver, embracing the Web Spinner). Very few on any tribe will really avoid corruption, though a lot will <u>think</u> to have avoided corruption.<br /> <br /> The Apocalypse can be averted, but for that the players will have to do something the Nation as a whole never could: actualy, trully learn with the past and make up for it. Of course, now they have so little numbers and time to redeem the entirety of Garou History...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:58:47-08:00","id":820517,"title":"","content":"If I ever did one it would be the Red Talons. They are by far the tribe closest to the Wyrm even if they think they aren't. They are more than willing to commit atrocities and create a massive schism between themselves and any other tribe in multiple ways. They deny a whole half of what they are which in some ways could be taken as an insult toward Gaia as she gave them their human half yet they shun her gift and then hypocritically use the heightened intelligence they get from said human half in order to wage a genocide against humanity. I love the Red Talons as a concept but they are technically the KKK of the Garou nation and not only are committing a slow mass suicide for themselves but are not learning from any of their past mistakes and in fact think those mistakes were good things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T07:48:46-08:00","id":820972,"title":"","content":"How come no one has considered the Wendigo? All that rage towards the White Man and not to mention their cannabalistic Totem.<br /> Or Uktena, maybe all that Banetending and secret rites finally pushed them over the edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a hr